## Third-party content

The repository quotes third-party copyrighted material under fair use / fair dealing for review, criticism, and scholarship:

- Court filings, government inquiry reports, and other primary public-record documents — public domain in their jurisdiction of origin or available under government-document licensing.
- Excerpts from journalistic and scholarly sources — quoted at fair-use length with full attribution per Chicago Manual of Style Notes-Bibliography 17th edition citation discipline.
- Translations from non-English primary sources — author's translations unless otherwise attributed.

The font files at `pipelines/print/fonts/` (EB Garamond, JetBrains Mono) carry their own SIL Open Font License terms in their respective `OFL.txt` files; the MIT license above does not override those.

---

## Authorship and attribution suggestion

For citation purposes, the recommended attribution form is:

> Li, Xiaolai. *No One Did It: Responsibility Laundering, from the Scapegoat to the Algorithm*. Source repository, 2026. <https://github.com/xiaolai/responsibility-laundering>

For derivative works using the apparatus (MIT) to build other books, attribution to the apparatus is appreciated but not required; attribution for prose excerpts (CC BY-NC) is required.
